From 60cde783fd4fa5a0f5b3c7fab00eda2b0c2ae8c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loukious <24696530+Loukious@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:28:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qcacld: initialize scan request n_channels before first use

__wlan_hdd_cfg80211_vendor_scan() assigned request->n_channels only
after the frequency fill loop, but every prior use of
request->channels[...] -- the address-of in the request->ssids setup
and the stores inside both fill loops -- is bounds-checked against
request->n_channels by UBSAN flexible-array instrumentation.
qdf_mem_malloc() does not zero the buffer, so those checks ran
against uninitialized heap garbage; when the garbage compared below
n_channels the code tripped brk #0x5512 (UBSAN array-bounds trap)
and, with panic_on_oops=1, rebooted the phone. WPS attacks from the
NetHunter chroot hit this on every try: their wpa_supplicant issues
a QCA vendor scan with SSIDs plus a frequency list.

Publish the allocation size into request->n_channels right after the
malloc, then shrink it to the filled count after the loop as before.

Change-Id: I349b5037b52e53bb7113420debdf3c74c077bf34
---
 .../wlan/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_scan.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qcom/opensource/wlan/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_scan.c b/qcom/opensource/wlan/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_scan.c
index 29c3a6b45bd..b6e08854971 100644
--- a/qcom/opensource/wlan/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_scan.c
+++ b/qcom/opensource/wlan/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_scan.c
@@ -1017,6 +1017,17 @@ static int __wlan_hdd_cfg80211_vendor_scan(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 	request = qdf_mem_malloc(len);
 	if (!request)
 		goto error;
+	/*
+	 * channels[] is bounds-instrumented against n_channels (flexible
+	 * array member), so every use of request->channels[...] -- including
+	 * the address-of below -- is checked against request->n_channels.
+	 * qdf_mem_malloc does not zero the buffer and the field was only
+	 * assigned after the fill loop, so the checks ran against
+	 * uninitialized heap garbage and could trip the UBSAN trap
+	 * (panic + reboot). Publish the allocation size before the first
+	 * use; it is shrunk to the filled count after the loop.
+	 */
+	request->n_channels = n_channels;
 	if (n_ssid)
 		request->ssids = (void *)&request->channels[n_channels];
 	request->n_ssids = n_ssid;
@@ -1064,6 +1075,11 @@ static int __wlan_hdd_cfg80211_vendor_scan(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 	if (!count)
 		goto error;
 
+	/*
+	 * Shrink to the number of entries actually filled: disabled channels
+	 * are skipped, so count <= n_channels. Downstream code reads this
+	 * field as the number of valid channels.
+	 */
 	request->n_channels = count;
 	count = 0;
 	if (tb[QCA_WLAN_VENDOR_ATTR_SCAN_SSIDS]) {
